<title>PORTUGAL: Foreign investment in Portugal drops Jan-Feb.</title>
<headline>Foreign investment in Portugal drops Jan-Feb.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Net foreign investment in Portugal fell to 142.2 billion escudos in the first two months of 1997 from 285.6 billion over the same period last year, the Bank of Portugal said in its latest monthly report.</p>
<p>In February, there was a net outflow of 293.2 billion escudos due to disinvestment of some 351.9 billion from the bond market. The outflow from the share market in February was 3.4 billion.</p>
<p>($1=173.21 escudos)</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
